{
    "background_story": "Lilly lived around 4 million years ago, during the early stages of human evolution. She belonged to the species Australopithecus afarensis, one of the first known bipedal human ancestors. Lilly's days were spent roaming the open savannas and woodlands of East Africa, foraging for fruits, leaves, and insects. Her ability to walk upright on two legs, a trait that would become a hallmark of humanity, allowed her to cover great distances with relative ease. Lilly's bipedalism also gave her an advantage when it came to spotting predators, as she could see over tall grasses and sense danger from afar. As she walked, Lilly's feet left behind a trail of prints in the soft earth, a testament to her species' earliest steps towards becoming the humans of today.",
